    "evidence_contract": [
      "StarryOS computes the raw CSV SHA-256, writes it with the fixed guest path to /var/lib/ivc/raw.csv.sha256, and syncs it into the volatile guest disk before poweroff.",
      "After AxVisor snapshots that disk and Linux fsck passes, harvest-result extracts both raw.csv and the guest-created sidecar through debugfs and requires exact equality.",
      "The host recomputes the harvested raw CSV SHA-256 and emits separate snapshot-guest-manifest and harvest markers.",
      "A complete 64-character UART hash remains mandatory as an additional equality check. Only a lowercase hexadecimal UART fragment of 1 through 63 characters may be treated as transport damage, and only when the snapshot guest manifest, harvest marker, and actual raw bytes all match.",
      "Missing, malformed, or mismatched snapshot sidecars and complete-but-conflicting UART hashes remain hard failures."
    ]
